Command: m
Effect : move characters to clipboard
Modes  : x, x-y, x@y, <string>

Examples:
m 5     - move 5 characters to clipboard starting at current char. pointer
m 3-10  - move characters 3 through 10 inclusive to clipboard
m 6@30  - move 6 characters starting at character 30 to clipboard
m <str> - move the next occurrence of the string <str> on the current line (if
          any) to the clipboard

Note: The command is basically the same as 'c' followed by 'd'.  Opening a new
      file does not erase the previous contents of the clipboard.  You can use
      this to cut and paste between files.  Also see the help on strings.


